       After creating a new PID namespace, it  is  useful  for  the  child  to
       change  its  root directory and mount a new procfs instance at _/_p_r_o_c so
       that tools such as ppss(1) work correctly.  If a new mount  namespace  is
       simultaneously  created  by including CCLLOONNEE__NNEEWWNNSS in the _f_l_a_g_s argument
       of cclloonnee(2) or uunnsshhaarree(2), then it isn’t necessary to change  the  root
       directory: a new procfs instance can be mounted directly over _/_p_r_o_c.

       From a shell, the command to mount _/_p_r_o_c is:

           $ mount -t proc proc /proc

       Calling rreeaaddlliinnkk(2) on the path _/_p_r_o_c_/_s_e_l_f yields the process ID of the
